    {
      "id": "p0062-b008",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Normally, the complexity of Undertale's script might've warranted two English-to-Japanese translators in order to achieve a timely release. Instead, 8-4 opted to take it slow and only go with one. This meant the game would take longer and cost more money to localize, but it also brought benefits with it:",
        "raw": "Normally, the complexity of Undertale's script might've warranted two\nEnglish-to-Japanese translators in order to achieve a timely release. Instead,\n8-4 opted to take it slow and only go with one. This meant the game would take\nlonger and cost more money to localize, but it also brought benefits with it:",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.29248671,
          0.63271429,
          0.90187891,
          0.7009
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
